module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.doctrine_safety_claim_stated_wider_than_the_census_that_delivers_it

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data doctrine_safety_claim_stated_wider_than_the_census_that_delivers_it: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "doctrine_safety_claim_stated_wider_than_the_census_that_delivers_it" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a DOCTRINE in the design authority states a safety property unconditionally while the mechanism that would deliver it ranges, BY SIGNED RULING, over a declared subset -- so a reader correctly following the doctrine infers a census the ruling deliberately does not provide** (INVALID STATE: a normative sentence of the form `in a fail-closed substrate X is guaranteed` stands in the document a reader consults FIRST, with no scope qualifier, while the executing mechanism that produces X admits its subjects by a roster an operator signed with a stated price. NOTHING IS HIDDEN AND NOTHING IS BROKEN -- the limitation is declared where it is enforced, counted, written to the disposition artifact and announced per run. THE DEFECT IS ONLY THE JOIN: the two facts live in two documents, one of which is prescriptive and silent about the other. HARM: the doctrine instructs an author to RELY on the mechanism instead of doing the work the mechanism does, so a product-layer migration is performed with no census at all and the author has followed the authority exactly. This is DESIGN section 4b(1) rung inflation applied to a doctrine rather than to an error class, and it is worse in the same way: an inflated doctrine never ranks for climbing, because the document says the guarantee is already there.)",

    "THE RULING IS NOT A HOLE AND THIS ROW DOES NOT TREAT IT AS ONE, which is the correction that produced this row's final shape. `v2.workflow.required_floor` states it directly above `required_gate_prefixes`: `THE REQUIRED GATE: A STATIC ROSTER, BY OPERATOR RULING (2026-08-29, THE CI BANKRUPTCY)`, priced on the last green whole-corpus run -- 11,996 witnesses folded, 27 minutes preparing 4,171 modules on one core, 32 more to fold, 87 wall minutes, against ~50 squash-merges a day and fifteen consecutive red runs on main from two integration collisions no PR could have seen. `the required gate is the compiler floor and nothing else; the rest of the corpus runs as receipts, not as merge conditions`, and `this roster is a constant the operator signed`. It is a declared rung drop, `gunbc.rung_drop` `required_gate_bankruptcy`, whose restoration trigger is the derived selection that replaces the constant. A site outside it is `DeclinedOutsideRequiredGate` -- counted, written to the disposition TSV, reported in the announcement, never silently skipped. So the coverage loss is DECLARED POLICY WITH A STATED PRICE. Widening the roster is not this row's remedy, is not proposed here, and re-tendering that trade uninvited would be re-litigating a signed ruling on worse evidence than it was made on.",

    "THE MEASURED INSTANCE, joined at identity and at a named head. DESIGN section 3's replacement-migration standing rule says of delete-first that `in a fail-closed substrate the deletion is the census -- every real dependent refuses loudly, so what breaks is exactly what was load-bearing`. gunbc#10994 renamed `unsized` to `undispatchable` on `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_program_view` `RemainingShape`. FIVE consumer sites in three modules kept the old spelling -- `test.claim.instrument_sandbox_witness_test` at two constructor sites, `test.claim.instrument_tuner_witness_test` at one, `test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_program_view_witness_test` at one constructor site and at one stale field READ in `witness_fixture_shape_exact_populations` -- and from that head onward those three modules could not resolve. At head 46b4ba130cd, where the declaration already reads `undispatchable` and the consumers still read `unsized`, run 34689263434 reported `required-witnesses-floor` SUCCESS (job 103541547386) and `required-witnesses-build` SUCCESS (job 103541547478). The five sites were found by a lane reading review 64526, not by any red, and repaired in commit 6d6a39fbbcc.",

    "THE DISCRIMINATOR THAT PROVES THIS IS COVERAGE AND NOT A WEAK TYPECHECKER, and it is the fact that makes the row a doctrine defect rather than a compiler defect: restoring the old spelling at one site yields `field 'unsized' not found in type 'RemainingShape'` together with `missing required field 'undispatchable'`. The substrate DOES refuse loudly. It simply never looked. None of the three module paths carries any of the 31 prefixes in `required_gate_prefixes`, every one of which is compiler-oriented -- `test.claim.payload_arm_excess_field_admission_test`'s own annotation states the intent as admitting `only compiler-oriented prefixes`, and the ruling names what is out: `nothing here is a product, fleet, deploy, secret, dashboard or roadmap witness`. `the deletion is the census` is therefore a true statement about the modules the gate compiles and a FALSE statement about every product-layer dependent -- roadmap, instrument, harness, spark, fabric, belt.",

    "THE SECOND HEAD, AND WHAT IT DOES AND DOES NOT ADD (receipt from eager-gull-33, authorised by bright-boar-435, 2026-09-12; every fact below re-verified here against the named commits rather than relayed). The same unrepaired state stands on a SECOND branch: gunbc#11014 at head 3b6f6c64b99 (`session/vivid-ant-470`) carries `undispatchable: Int` on the declaration and the same five old-spelling references in the same three modules, the same 4 constructor sites plus the field read `lv.remaining.unsized` in `witness_fixture_shape_exact_populations`. That branch shares no lineage with `session/eager-gull-33` -- their merge base is main at 8bc6ec1e0d8 -- and the break is also present at an earlier head of the first branch, b884668e8e2, whose run 34680031177 was likewise green. WHAT THIS IS NOT, and the distinction is worth the sentence because the obvious reading overstates it: this is NOT the rename being authored twice by two uncoordinated lanes. Both branches CONTAIN THE SAME RENAME COMMIT, 7e17bff1d27, so there is one authorship event carried onto two branches. What is genuinely doubled is the thing this row is about -- THE NUMBER OF INDEPENDENT OCCASIONS THE REQUIRED GATE HAD TO REFUSE A NON-RESOLVING CORPUS AND DID NOT. Three heads on two branches, every one green. A count of authorship events would be one; a count of missed censuses is three.",

    "THE COUNT IS FIVE REFERENCES AND NOT FIVE CONSTRUCTOR SITES, and the distinction is recorded because it was gotten wrong once by a careful measurer and would mislead any later reader. bright-boar-435 first measured four by grepping `unsized:` WITH THE COLON, which matches only record-literal fields and silently misses `lv.remaining.unsized`; the count was corrected by line number. The two are not interchangeable: repairing four constructors and stopping leaves the read unresolved, and the compiler reports them as different errors -- a missing required field at the literal versus an unknown field at the access. A pattern chosen for one syntactic form is not a population over the semantic one, and that miscount landed inside the receipt of a row whose whole subject is a denominator read wider than the mechanism that produced it.",

    "WHAT THE GREEN PROVES, STATED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS BECAUSE ONLY ONE OF THEM IS USUALLY SAID. IT DOES prove that the modules the required lane compiles resolve and that their claims pass. IT DOES NOT prove that the `.dag` corpus resolves: a module absent from the lane's prepared closure can fail to resolve indefinitely and redden nothing. The gap is not recoverable from the verdict, because the run announces the phases it owns and not the modules it did not compile -- so a reader cannot separate COVERAGE from CORRECTNESS by looking at a green, which is precisely the separation the doctrine's unqualified sentence tells them they do not need to make.",

    "THE POSITIVE CONTROL, AND IT IS WHAT MAKES THE DISCRIMINATOR ENROLMENT RATHER THAN ERROR KIND (measured here on the named head, not relayed). gunbc#11162 at ff6c853af9b added `import std.token_count { token_count }` to `dag/test/claim/spark/spark_serving_offer_route_witness_test.dag` for a module that does not exist. The required floor CAUGHT IT: run 34697340022, job 103562976623, `unresolved import: module 'std.token_count' not found (imported by 'test.claim.spark.spark_serving_offer_route_witness_test')`, `floor_class=structural`, `blockers=1`, and the job concluded failure. `test.claim.spark.` matches NO entry in the 31 prefixes -- exactly like the three modules in this row's instance -- so gate-roster membership cannot be what separates the caught case from the uncaught one. WHAT SEPARATES THEM IS THAT THE WITNESS FILE WAS ITSELF EDITED: the diff changed test identities in that module, so `edits.edited_test_fns` enrolled it, preparation compiled it, and the refusal fired. The `RemainingShape` consumers were edited by nobody -- the rename was in a different file -- so they were enrolled by nothing and compiled by nothing. A green is bounded by ENROLMENT, and a missing MODULE in an unedited product-layer consumer would go green exactly as the missing FIELD did.",

    "THE SECOND POSITIVE CONTROL, AND IT CLOSES THE LAST READING THE FIRST ONE LEAVES OPEN (measured here on the named head, not relayed; receipt routed by bright-boar-435 from keen-owl-253). The first control is a STRUCTURAL refusal -- an import of a module that does not exist -- so it still admits the reading that the gate catches only structural defects and that semantic evaluation is where the weakness lies. gunbc#11162 at 7514dd45ad594172ab9fbe12849719f8b248d14e refutes that: run 34699476983, floor job 103571288591, `claims_failed=4`, and three of the four are witnesses that COMPILE AND RESOLVE PERFECTLY and assert nothing -- `every_use_program_is_not_engaged_and_names_its_basis` reading its standings off a permit arm nothing can admit any more, and `a_non_first_party_use_refuses_as_unsupported` and `a_superseded_posture_makes_the_first_party_sanction_stale` both greened by a route-facts refusal firing before the one they name. The floor evaluated them and returned `Bool(false)`. So the gate does FULL SEMANTIC WORK on what it prepares, and the blind spot is not a class of error at all -- it is a class of MODULE.",

    "THE RUN NAMES THE DISCRIMINATOR IN ITS OWN VOCABULARY, which is the strongest form this receipt could take. The floor log carries `identity=test.claim.spark.spark_first_party_serving_witness_test.every_use_program_is_not_engaged_and_names_its_basis standing=planned-without-terminal-verdict disposition=planned_as_changed_witness outcome=failed`. `planned_as_changed_witness` IS the enrolment clause: `test.claim.spark.` matches none of the 31 prefixes, so nothing about the roster planned these three -- the author was editing their file, and that alone is why they were evaluated. The author states the counterfactual from the inside: had those three witnesses lived in a file the diff did not touch, they would have gone green forever while asserting nothing. That is this row's invalid state reported by someone who hit it from the other side.",

    "WHAT THIS RECEIPT DOES NOT CLAIM, AND THE BOUNDARY IS THE REASON IT CAN BE CARRIED HERE AT ALL. The DEFECT those three witnesses carry -- an assertion that cannot discriminate, green on an arm nothing reaches -- is not this row's and is not claimed by it; it belongs with [[discriminating_arm_built_but_never_enrolled]] and [[executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing]], and folding it in would be this row absorbing a neighbour on the strength of a shared specimen. What this row takes from the specimen is ONLY the enrolment fact: same gate, same non-allowlisted prefix, full semantic evaluation, opposite outcome, and the single variable is whether the diff touched the file. A row carrying only negative receipts invites the reading that the gate is weak; with both controls it says the truer and sharper thing, which is that the gate does real work on what it prepares and cannot see the consumers a change does not touch.",

    "THE MECHANISM IS NOW MEASURED ON THE INSTANCE ITSELF AND NO LONGER INFERRED, which retires the one gap this row carried. Earlier readings of this class reasoned from an absence -- the break did not redden, therefore the modules cannot have been compiled -- and that inference was correctly retracted by its author as an over-assertion. It did not need to be inferred: the required floor PUBLISHES the per-identity disposition as the `required-floor-disposition` artifact (`required_floor_disposition.tsv`), retrievable with `gh run download <run> -n required-floor-disposition`. On run 34689263434, the green run over the broken head 46b4ba130cd, EVERY identity of all three modules carries `declined_outside_gate_closure` with `outcome=not_executed` -- the sole identity of `test.claim.instrument_sandbox_witness`, the sole identity of `test.claim.instrument_tuner_witness`, and all twelve of `test.claim.roadmap_program_view_witness`. That run's summary reads `total=18592 planned=3770 declined_outside_gate_closure=13522`. The three modules were never prepared, so they were never compiled, so nothing about them could refuse. The claim is now a reading of the instrument's own output.",

    "PREPARED AND EXECUTED ARE TWO DIFFERENT GUARANTEES AND THE ARTIFACT SEPARATES THEM AT IDENTITY GRAIN -- which is what keeps this row's subject from being confused with a neighbouring and equally real gap (refinement from keen-owl-253 via bright-boar-435, verified here on the artifact). On run 34704198398 ONE module, `test.claim.spark.spark_serving_offer_route_witness_test`, carries NINE identities under TWO dispositions: eight `planned_as_changed_witness` / `passed`, and `an_observed_route_binds_and_the_offer_carries_it` at `declined_outside_required_gate` / `not_executed`. The author edited eight identities and not the ninth, so PLANNING is per IDENTITY, not per file. But the ninth's disposition is `declined_outside_required_gate`, which this row's mechanism receipt distinguishes precisely: PREPARED, not executed. Its module was compiled. So an untouched identity inside a touched file has no ASSERTION evaluated, while a module with any touched identity IS compiled and a non-resolving reference anywhere in it WOULD refuse. THE TWO BLIND SPOTS ARE THEREFORE NESTED AND NOT THE SAME: an unevaluated assertion in a compiled module, and this row's subject, a module that is never compiled at all. Reading the identity-grain fact as though it governed compilation would widen this row past its evidence.",

    "SO THE EVIDENCE FOR COVERAGE IS THE ARTIFACT AND NEVER THE LOG, and this deserves its own sentence because the failure is this row's own shape one level down. A green floor log reports the run's totals and its non-passing lines; a witness that passed and a witness that was never selected are both simply ABSENT from it, and absence cannot distinguish them. Anyone establishing coverage from the log alone reads never-looked as passed -- which is the exact confusion the doctrine's unqualified sentence produces at the level above. The per-identity dispositions and outcomes are published, joined, and retrievable; the answer exists and is simply not the artifact a reader reaches for.",

    "THE PLAUSIBLE WRONG READING, RECORDED BECAUSE TWO CAREFUL PEOPLE REACHED IT FROM THE SAME TWO DATA POINTS AND A THIRD WOULD TOO. Set the caught case beside the uncaught one and the obvious story is DECLARATION GRAIN: a green proves no unresolved module IMPORT and proves nothing about whether every NAME resolves, so imports are walled and declaration references are not. It fits both specimens, it is falsifiable, and it is WRONG -- it sends a reader hunting a typechecker gap that does not exist, and it understates the blind spot by implying an unedited consumer with a broken IMPORT would be caught. It was refuted not by another run outcome but by reading `required_gate_prefixes` and `closure_seeds` in source, which is the only place the discriminator is visible. THE STANDING LESSON, and it is this row's own subject turned on its own investigation: a mechanism inferred from which runs happened to redden is a story fitted to outcomes, and the outcomes of a SELECTED population cannot distinguish what the selector excluded from what the checker tolerated. Both readings were assembled from greens and reds; only the source read settled it.",

    "TWO MECHANISM FACTS A READER NEEDS, because together they are why the author of the rename could not have been warned. FIRST: CHANGING AN AUTHORITY DOES NOT ENROL ITS UNCHANGED WITNESS CONSUMERS. `required_floor_runner` `closure_seeds` seeds preparation from the required-gate prefixes, the floor's runtime-authority modules, the modules containing SELECTED CHANGED test identities (`edits.edited_test_fns`), and the wet-schedule entries. Editing a type pulls in no witness that merely uses it, so the perturbation and the dependent are never joined. SECOND: DISCOVERY AND PREPARATION ARE DIFFERENT RANGES. The runner discovers declarations corpus-wide but prepares strictly, and `DeclinedOutsideGateClosure` (discovered, NOT prepared) is a distinct disposition from `DeclinedOutsideRequiredGate` (prepared, not executed). So EVERY DISCOVERED IDENTITY RECEIVED A DISPOSITION is not EVERY DEPENDENT WAS CHECKED: a complete-looking identity census coexists with incomplete semantic checking, and that is the sentence a reader most needs and the one no artifact says.",

    "THE RECOGNITION RULE, phrased so it fires on prose and not on code: for every unconditional safety sentence in an authority, NAME THE EXECUTING MECHANISM THAT PRODUCES IT AND THEN NAME ITS SUBJECT. If the mechanism admits its subject by an authored roster, prefix list, allowlist, or any membership test that is not the whole corpus, the sentence is scoped and the authority must carry the scope -- even, and especially, when the narrowing is a signed ruling, because a declared limitation is exactly the kind a reader assumes someone else already reconciled with the doctrine. The tell is a sentence whose subject noun is the SUBSTRATE (`in a fail-closed substrate`, `every real dependent`, `the compiler refuses`) beside a mechanism whose subject is a SELECTION. A doctrine may describe a property of the language; it may not describe a property of the GATE as though it were a property of the language.",

    "WHY THE REPAIR IS THE WORDING AND NOT THE ROSTER, which is the part a reader is most likely to get backwards. The invalid state is the UNQUALIFIED SENTENCE, and it is invalid whatever the gate's width: a gate that admitted the whole corpus today would still leave the doctrine asserting a property of the substrate rather than of a mechanism, and the next cost ruling that narrows the gate -- the 2026-08-29 ruling being the receipt that such rulings happen -- would silently re-open it. The honest repair scopes the claim to the census the gate actually performs and names what a product-layer migration must do instead, which is to enumerate its consumers by hand before deleting the root.",

    "BOUNDARY AGAINST [[witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red]], WHICH OWNS THE MECHANISM AND IS NOT THIS CLASS, and the distinction is the whole reason a second identity is minted. That row's second specimen is structurally the same event -- gunbc#10966 added five required fields to `extdeps.github.workflow_runs` `WorkflowRun` and four literals in a gate-excluded claim file stopped compiling with the floor green -- and its widened trigger (compile every claim-root file AND every construction site of a type whose declared field set changed, regardless of gate closure) would have caught the five `RemainingShape` sites too. So those sites are a further specimen of THAT row's population and no new mechanism is claimed for them here. What is new is that the DESIGN AUTHORITY tells an author the opposite: that row's subject is a witness file that is silently absent, and its repair is a compile step; this row's subject is a normative sentence, and its repair is words in `gunbc.design_document`. Landing that row's trigger in full leaves the doctrine's wording exactly as unqualified, and correcting the wording executes nothing -- disjoint repairs, which is the test that settles it.",

    "BOUNDARY AGAINST [[required_lane_green_over_a_population_it_never_offered]], WHICH IS THE NEAREST DENOMINATOR ROW. There the defect is that a terminal verdict is built from the offered subset and does not disclose the identities it declined to offer, and the repair is a total disposition over the declared universe. That repair is about the RUN'S REPORT. The present class survives it untouched: a floor verdict naming every declined identity would still be read beside a design sentence promising that deletion is a census, and the author of a product-layer rename does not read floor verdicts before renaming a field -- they read the doctrine. Conversely, correcting the doctrine leaves every verdict exactly as it is. Same excluded population, different artifact, disjoint repairs.",

    "BOUNDARY AGAINST [[stale_present_tense_coverage_claim_in_the_authority_consulted_first]], WHICH SHARES THE LOCATION AND NOT THE HISTORY. There a sentence is written AT A DE-ENROLMENT to discharge a reviewer's objection -- `enforcement is NOT reduced: it executes per-PR via X` -- and it becomes false because X is on no executing path; the sentence was once a live compensation and the class is its decay. Here nothing decayed: the doctrine was stated at substrate grain from the beginning, and the ruling that narrowed the gate landed later and elsewhere without touching it. A staleness detector re-checking every coverage sentence against today's executing paths would not fire, because the sentence names no consumer to check. What is missing is a SCOPE, not a refresh.",

    "BOUNDARY AGAINST [[check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim]], which is the same asymmetry one layer down. There a CHECK is cited for a population wider than the one its implementation ranges over, and the repair is to widen the check or narrow its citation. Here there is no defective check to widen: the substrate's refusal is total and correct at every site it reaches, and the floor's selection is a priced ruling rather than an accident of first implementation -- which is precisely the distinction that row makes load-bearing when it says the narrowing `is never a decision`. Here it WAS a decision. The narrowness lives only in the JOIN between a doctrine's stated subject and a mechanism's signed subject, which is why the population is prose in `gunbc.design_document` rather than any executing declaration.",

    "THE POPULATION IS NAMED BY ITS PRODUCER AND NOT TRANSCRIBED, because a count of unqualified safety sentences copied here would rot beside the document it describes. The candidates are the sentences of `gunbc.design_document` that assert a guarantee in the present tense over a substrate-grain subject; the mechanisms they could rest on are the required lanes rostered at `gunbc.witness_floor_workflow` `required_lanes_roster` and the prefix roster at `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_gate_prefixes`, read beside the standing drops at `gunbc.rung_drop`. `the deletion is the census` is the one adjudicated. No number is recorded here and none may be quoted from this row.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable, and the mitigation is that a reader happened to read a review. Nothing holds this class today: the doctrine is prose, no `Accepted` program can read it (DESIGN section 4c), and the one instrument that could have contradicted it -- the required floor -- reports SUCCESS by signed construction over the population where the doctrine is false. CEILING: 2, mechanically preventable, and the ceiling is honestly 2 and not higher because the subject is an authored English sentence whose intended scope is not derivable from any modeled fact; what IS derivable is the gate's admitted subject, so a doctrine sentence can be REQUIRED to cite the mechanism it rests on and that citation can be joined against the mechanism's actual subject. Making the unqualified sentence unwritable would need the doctrine itself modeled as a claim with a declared subject, which is not a capability this repo has or has planned.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, STATED AS A CAPABILITY AND NOT AS AN ARTIFACT: a design-document guarantee sentence carries a DECLARED MECHANISM REFERENCE and a DECLARED SUBJECT, and a check joins that subject against the mechanism's own admitted subject and refuses, typed and located, when the declared subject is wider. SUFFICIENT FOR: every unconditional guarantee sentence in the authority, not only this one. Editing the wording of `the deletion is the census` repairs the single instance and fires NOTHING -- the next doctrine written at substrate grain over a rostered mechanism is exactly as dark, which is why the wording repair is not offered here as the trigger.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
